#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# parametric_nd_solve

#% text
# `parametric_nd_solve(eqs, y, [t, t0, t1], [p1, ..., pm])` solves the differential equations `eqs` numerically as a function of the parameters `p1, ..., pm`, giving `[y -> f]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `f` is the parametric function of `parametric_n_dsolve_value`: `f(v1, ..., vm)` is the interpolating function of the solution with the parameters set to the numbers `v1, ..., vm`.

#% item
# A list of unknowns gives a rule for each.

#% item
# The options are those of `n_dsolve`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sol = parametric_nd_solve([y'(t) == a*y(t), y(0) == 1], y, [t, 0, 10], [a])

#% cell
y1 = rewrite(y(1), sol)

#% cell
y1(1)
#% output
#= 2.71828183393394

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `parametric_nd_solve_value`, `parametric_n_dsolve_value`, `n_dsolve`
